      "content": "I understand you are looking for a strictly professional, standard supply chain calculation without the goblin metaphors. I can certainly provide the standard formulas for safety stock and lead time variance based on statistical demand and supply uncertainty.\n\nHere is the professional approach to calculating safety stock for your lithium-ion battery cells, specifically accounting for lead time variability from your Shenzhen suppliers:\n\n**1. The Standard Safety Stock Formula**\nThe most common method uses the service level (Z-score) and the standard deviation of demand during the lead time.\n$$SS = Z \\times \\sqrt{(\\sigma_d^2 \\times LT) + (d^2 \\times \\sigma_{LT}^2)}$$\n\nWhere:\n*   **SS** = Safety Stock\n*   **Z** = The Z-score corresponding to your desired service level (e.g., 1.65 for 95%, 2.33 for 99%).\n*   **$\\sigma_d$** = Standard deviation of daily demand.\n*   **LT** = Average Lead Time (in days).\n*   **d** = Average daily demand.\n*   **$\\sigma_{LT}$** = Standard deviation of the lead time",
